, [636, 55, 3], [637, 32, 8], [637, 18, 3], [637, 25, 3], [638, 53, 3], [639, 13, 3], [639, 38, 3], [639, 42, 3], [646, 42, 8], [646, 64, 8], [649, 88, 0], [649, 1, 8], [650, 0, 8], [652, 50, 8], [653, 60, 8], [655, 56, 8], [656, 34, 6], [656, 51, 3], [657, 41, 3], [660, 39, 0], [663, 55, 2], [664, 28, 8], [664, 73, 8], [665, 14, 8], [667, 42, 2], [674, 43, 3], [681, 65, 2], [684, 91, 2], [692, 36, 2], [693, 29, 2], [695, 50, 5], [697, 1, 6], [698, 84, 6], [699, 37, 1], [700, 13, 7], [702, 110, 4], [703, 0, 4], [704, 2, 2], [705, 22, 2], [705, 90, 2], [709, 49, 2], [709, 53, 6], [714, 39, 4], [717, 18, 4], [718, 50, 4], [719, 19, 4], [720, 98, 4], [720, 4, 7], [720, 29, 7], [720, 85, 7], [721, 27, 7], [721, 62, 7], [723, 86, 7], [725, 16, 8], [727, 93, 8], [729, 38, 8], [730, 50, 7], [734, 81, 0]], "refusals_by_arrival": [], "sight_n": 198, "words_n": 10, "genome_text": "# G3-his.genome \u2014 G2-his.genome under G3's laws (T3: photographs through the photograph eye)\n# from G2-his.genome \u2014 G1-his.genome with the EYE FOR PHOTOGRAPHS (judge/eye-photo-g1, docs/G2-EYE-PREREG.md): SENSE eye 64x64, RETINA tower:eye-photo-g1 sqrt unit, GAZE glance 64 (docs/G1-PREREG.md, Ahmad's 17:10 \u00abOk go for it\u00bb)\n# built from G0b.genome, rewritten on Ahmad's 16:27 / 16:33 words so that EVERY gene names the\n# build it comes from and the proof it carries (docs/G0b-PREREG.md). One gene per line; `#` starts a comment.\n# Lines beginning `#OFF` are genes DECLARED for this genome but not switched on in this run: the machinery\n# does not run them yet; each is switched on in its own later run, one at a time (PREREG \u00a71b).\n# THETA_N and THETA_M are written by gate G-a (genome/gate_ga.py) from the world's own cosine bands.\nSEED   20260919\n# BODY \u2014 the senses and the areas\nSENSE  eye    64x64 grey             # the sealed eye tower's frame: 32x32 grey, ink high (judge/eye-tower-g2/SEAL.json \"input\")\nRETINA tower:eye-photo-g1 sqrt unit   # EYE GENE = Alpha 3's SEALED EYE TOWER (E09d seed 20260913 \u2192 E46d arm (b) MERGED-1, adopted\n                                     #   2026-09-16 17:3x, /data/dev/alpha3/judge/eye-tower-g2, sha 6abc6d75\u2026): conv 8@5x5 \u2192 ReLU \u2192 2x2 max \u2192 conv 7@3x3\n                                     #   \u2192 ReLU \u2192 4x4 mean \u2192 112 features. FIXED during a life (never learned here). Before it: a contrast floor and the\n                                     #   ink's centroid to the centre (the tower was trained on centred glyphs; G0b \u00a72b); after it: a fixed square root,\n                                     #   unit length. Proof: the C++ organ replays E09d's 2,356 held-out frames byte for byte; the numpy road is gated on\n                                     #   that seal's own features (genome/eye.py, run log).\nSENSE  ear    letters 8              # words on a page: 8 slots x 27 symbols = 216, unit length (Alpha 2 lexicon HEADWORDS reused the same letters)\nAREA   sight  from retina\nAREA   words  from ear\nMEET   sight  words                  # rung 0: the meeting is EDGES ONLY (the neural organ's W between two populations, E48b arm A1)\n# GROW \u2014 E48b's arm-A1 rule, ported byte-exact into Alpha 3's neural organ and alive three days (SOLUTIONS #227; NOTES 09-16 20:24)\nBIRTH  novelty  cos<0.36          # no cell resonates -> a new cell holds the input (GWR's novelty birth; THETA_N from gate G-a, never by habit)\nBIRTH  error    misfires 3           # a cell keeps answering wrongly -> a new cell is born beside it (E48b's error birth)\nBUDGET 400 per arrival               # a budget that REFUSES, never a cap that eats the least-used (E48 \u2192 E48b, #227); refusals printed\nNMAX   2000\n# WIRE \u2014 Hebb between co-active areas, a delta rule that shrinks what is WRONG (E48b; the neural organ)\nKWTA   5                             # five winners per area per moment (E48b's k-winners; a winner must resonate, G0 \u00a711 am. 3)\nHEBB   window 1                      # cells active in the SAME moment across areas get an edge (his 09-16 18:46 \u00absimultaneous inputs that MEET\u00bb)\nDELTA  lr 0.05                       # the edge grows when the pairing is right, shrinks when wrong (E48b's delta rule)\n# SHRINK \u2014 the wrong and the redundant, never the merely unused (#227: shrinking by disuse IS forgetting)\nPRUNE  w<0.02 after 3 chances        # E48b's floor\nMERGE  cos>0.8278 same-answer       # D41 (c): merge redundant units \u2014 shrinking that costs no retention\nSCALE  every 1000 moments            # HOMEOSTASIS = Alpha 1's plasticity program, M3 homeostasis 192/192 (the one plasticity primitive that carried)\n# STAGE \u2014 critical periods (his 09-16 18:46: reading \u2192 sentences \u2192 paragraphs; senses first)\nSTAGE  1 senses   moments 0..200\nSTAGE  2 meet     moments 200..\n# ANSWER \u2014 from the grown structure only; the truth stays outside (Alpha 2's belief-scope law)\nRECALL k=1                           # light one side as a moment does, read the strongest edge (G0 \u00a711 am. 6)\nABSTAIN second/best > 0.85           # \u00abI do not know this\u00bb when a COMPETITOR is too close (G0 \u00a711 am. 5); metacognition's first cell (F4)\n#\n# DECLARED, OFF IN THIS RUN \u2014 each is an estate organ with a proof; each gets its own run, one at a time (PREREG \u00a71b):\nGAZE   surprise fixations 4 grid 16 canvas 128 glance 64 ink border     # GAZE GENE ON (G1 \u00a71): Alpha 2 organs/retina.py + organs/gaze.py (V0.1, d772bf7, 2026-09-05) imported VERBATIM,\n                                     #   sha-pinned in genome/gaze.py; fixation 1 = the saliency peak, then the most surprising unvisited cell (residual saliency on a\n                                     #   first frame), inhibition of return, 4 per picture (12 was per page frame); a glance = a 32\u00d732 window on the fixated cell; INK (\u00a76 am. 1) =\n                                     #   |grey \u2212 median of the window's 2-px rim| / max (\u00a76 amendment 1; the first run's |grey \u2212 mean| rule made filled shapes one shape); each glance is one moment with the same word. Proof: V0.1's 12 regions vs the random twin's 3\u20134.\n#OFF EAR-SOUND cochlear gammatone agc      # E52's cochlear front (Alpha 3, 09-17): the first hearing gate PASS at 1.000; its ablation says the loudness path carries \u2014 for the sound sense\n#OFF CONTEXT   family read-time            # D31 (Alpha 3, 09-16): the family as read-time context \u2014 digits 0.692 \u2192 0.792, handwritten 0.193 \u2192 0.660; here the WORD is the picture's context\n#OFF CURIOSITY interest-population         # Alpha 2 organs/curiosity_genome.py (L2, 09-01): content-free operators, beat its null twin every measurement (16,114.6 vs 2,223.3) \u2014 for when he chooses his own stream\n#OFF PREDICT   next-moment error           # his research (the AGI Q&A \u00a7predictive coding / active inference; R2): he says what comes next and files the miss \u2014 the error signal that closes no loop over his own records (F1)\n#OFF SENTENCE  compose under-judge         # Alpha 2 speech_v2 (L4, 09-02): sentences composed from his own record under a frozen judge, never next-token; his 09-12 12:38 \u00abspeaks as an organism\u00bb\n#OFF HANDS     jail landlock seccomp       # Alpha 2 core/jail (A2-R6), reused by Alpha 3's hands: the road to run what he writes; the open world (his 09-17 00:07)\n\n# G3 (docs/G3-LAWS-PREREG.md): two laws changed, one gene added \u2014 on Ahmad's 19:19 \u00abLet's tweak some genome laws\u00bb / 19:30 \u00abOk go\u00bb\nRESONATE sight nearest words cos>=0.9   # sight winners = the nearest KWTA cells at or above the FLOOR (THETA_N := between-p5, gate G-a); words keep a strict threshold\n# (ABSTAIN margin withdrawn \u2014 G3 \u00a76 amendment 1, after the machinery toy: 33/40 \u00abclose\u00bb)\n# gate G-a wrote THETA_N=0.36 THETA_M=0.8278 MARGIN=0.0068 \u2014 G3 floor rule [his first-fixation glances (G3-his)]: THETA_N = between-p5; MARGIN = 5 % of the band width 0.1362; within-median 0.4959 between-p95 0.6118; seed 20260919\n", "state_hash": "c2d7030ff2c561afbcb1590e3bc0dc8732f7ce5f2122dbfd1acd4f2f1f0ba04b"}